<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js" integrity="sha384-3I5fS0K6xV4f5V4U5KX5A3m0qQdJ1B9p2z0qK5F5x6z8V5v5k5v5v5" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Times+New+Roman:wght@400;600&amp;display=swap');

        body {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background: #f4f4f4;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: flex-start;
            min-height: 100vh;
            line-height: 1.3;
        }

        .document {
            width: 800px;
            max-width: 95%;
            background: white;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
            margin: 40px auto;
            padding: 60px 70px 80px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            position: relative;
        }

        .document::before {
            content: '';
            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            right: 0;
            bottom: 0;
            pointer-events: none;
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 9999px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);
        }

        .header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 50px;
            font-size: 22px;
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: 1.5px;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
            padding-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .section {
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            position: relative;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-size: 14px;
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            border-left: 3px solid #000;
            padding-left: 12px;
        }

        .text-block {
            margin-bottom: 18px;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        .text-block p {
            margin: 0 0 12px 0;
            text-indent: 0;
        }

        .indent {
            text-indent: 20px;
        }

        .centered {
            text-align: center;
            margin: 25px 0;
        }

        .right {
            text-align: right;
        }

        .list-item {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
            padding-left: 20px;
            text-indent: -20px;
        }

        .placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 320px;
            background: #f9f9f9;
            border: 2px dashed #aaa;
            margin: 25px 0;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            flex-direction: column;
            color: #666;
            font-style: italic;
            position: relative;
        }

        .placeholder::before {
            content: attr(data-caption);
            text-align: center;
        }

        .small-caps {
            font-variant: small-caps;
        }

        .signature {
            width: 180px;
            margin-top: 40px;
            border-top: 1px solid #000;
            padding-top: 8px;
        }

        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }

        td, th {
            border: 1px solid #000;
            padding: 8px 12px;
            vertical-align: top;
        }

        .math {
            display: block;
            text-align: center;
            margin: 25px 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="document">
        <div class="header">DOCUMENT HEADER</div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 1</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>This is the first paragraph of the document. It demonstrates justified text alignment and normal paragraph spacing.</p>
                <p class="indent">The second paragraph is indented as per standard formatting conventions.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 2</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>Here is a short sentence with a [?] uncertain character and some [illegible] text that could not be read.</p>
                <p>This block shows how unclear segments are marked in brackets.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 3</div>
            <div class="centered">
                <p>A centered heading appears here.</p>
                <p class="small-caps">Small capital letters example.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="right">
                <p>Right-aligned text block.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 4</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>This is a numbered list:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li class="list-item">First item in the ordered list.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Second item with [illegible] text.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Third item.</li>
                </ol>

                <p>And an unordered list:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li class="list-item">Bullet point one.</li>
                    <li class="list-item">Bullet point two with a math equation: \( x^2 + y^2 = z^2 \)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 5</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>A display math equation:</p>
                <div class="math">
                    $$\int_{0}^{\infty} e^{-x^2} \, dx = \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}$$
                </div>
                <p>Inline math example: \( a + b = c \)</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 6</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>This paragraph is followed by a table:</p>
            </div>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Header 1</th>
                    <th>Header 2</th>
                    <th>Header 3</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Cell 1</td>
                    <td>Cell 2</td>
                    <td>Cell 3</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>[illegible]</td>
                    <td>Cell 5</td>
                    <td>Cell 6</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 7</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>Signature area:</p>
                <div class="signature"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 8</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>This is the last section with a placeholder for an image or diagram that appears in the original document layout.</p>
                <div class="placeholder" data-caption="[Diagram: centered - placeholder for chart or image]"></div>
                <p>Another placeholder for a photo or illustration placed below.</p>
                <div class="placeholder" data-caption="[Photo: bottom-right]"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <div class="section-title">Section 9</div>
            <div class="text-block">
                <p>Final paragraph demonstrating multi-column simulation if needed, but here it remains single-column for simplicity.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
